<?php declare(strict_types=1);require_once __DIR__.'/includes/header.php';?><main><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Security</div><h1>Security baseline.</h1><p>The project uses server-side validation, secure sessions, CSRF tokens, and protected file handling.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container article"><div class="article-body"><p>Security is implemented across the request lifecycle. Public input is validated on every form, HTML is escaped on output, and state-changing requests require an authenticated CSRF token.</p><h2>Passwords</h2><p>Password hashes are generated through PHP’s password hashing API. Plain-text passwords are never written to the users data file.</p><h2>Sessions</h2><p>Sessions are regenerated after authentication and use HTTP-only cookies. Production instances should enable HTTPS and the secure cookie flag.</p><h2>File handling</h2><p>Installer uploads are limited by size, extension, MIME type, filename sanitization, and random server filenames. Executable uploads are stored outside the web root.</p><h2>Production checklist</h2><p>Set a strong administrator password, enable HTTPS, configure a strict production error handler, restrict writable paths, and keep the upload directory outside the public document root.</p></div></div></section></main><?php require_once __DIR__.'/includes/footer.php'; ?>
